---
title: Pork cassoulet
description: Perfect for using up stray bits and pieces from the fridge, this pork and bean stew is rich, warming and cheap to prepare
time required: 2 hours 45 minutes
cook time: 2 hours 30 minutes
course: Dinner, Main course, Supper
nutrition:
  calories: 501 calories
  fat: 30 grams fat
  saturated fat: 11 grams saturated fat
  carbohydrates: 26 grams carbohydrates
  sugar: 6 grams sugar
  protein: 28 grams protein
  fiber: 8 grams fiber
  sodium: 2.1 milligram of sodium
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/jacks-pork-cassoulet
cuisine: French
author: Jack Monroe
servings: 4
prep time: 15 minutes
---

Heat oven to 275°F. 
Put a large #Dutch Oven{} (with a tight-fitting lid) on a high heat.
Add @duck fat{4%tbsp}(or lard) and assorted @pork{12%oz}(diced) - a mixture of bacon, sausage, and diced pork works well.

Cook for a few mins to seal the edges, giving it a quick stir to cook evenly. 
Reduce the heat to low, add @onion{1}(halved and sliced), @garlic{10%cloves}(peeled), @carrot{1}(thinly sliced),
and @fennel seeds{1%tsp}, and cook gently to soften the veg for a few mins.

Pour over @red wine vinegar{2%tbsp}, scraping any meaty bits off the bottom of the pan.
Add @stock{2.5%cups}, @tomato paste{1%tbsp}, and @rosemary{1%stalk}(leaves picked and chopped)
and @parsley{1}(small handful, finely chopped).

Bring to a boil and simmer for ~{10%minutes}, then season with @salt and @pepper, cover with a lid
and put into the oven for ~{120%minutes}, removing the lid for the final hour of cooking.
Stir occasionally. With ~{30%minutes} to go add @navy beans{14%oz}(drained, or cannellini beans).

Remove the pan from the oven and heat the broiler.
Scatter the top with the remaining @rosemary{1%stalk}(leaves picked and chopped), @parsley{1}(small handful, finely chopped),
and @breadcrumbs{few%tbsp}, drizzle a little @oil{} over the top.
Return the pan to the oven for ~{5-10%minutes}, until the breadcrumbs are golden.

= Serving =
Serve with @crusty bread{} and @green vegetables{}.